<!--Program — CreateTransformation
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.transformer.program.CreateTransformation-->
<program:CreateTransformation xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:program="org.blockml.bml.transformer.program">

  <baseType>
    workflow:ModelTransformation(program:CreateTransformation.Parameters, type:Text)
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A program that creates a new ModelTransformation
  </is>
  <properties>
    <description override="true">
      <value>A program that creates a new ModelTransformation</value>
    </description>
    <status override="true" type="workflow:ExecutionStatus">
      <value>Pending</value>
    </status>
    <createdAt override="true" type="type:DateTime">
      <value>2026-08-30T01:40:20</value>
    </createdAt>
    <template override="true" type="type:Boolean">
      <value>true</value>
    </template>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <operations override="true">
      <composition>
        <workflow:AgenticOperation name="Create Transformation Block" status="Pending" captureOutput="true">
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask>
              <instructions>Create a new ModelTransformation block with the FQN:

${ #this.parameters.fqn }

Use `org.blockml.bml.transformer.program.CreateTransformation` as the template for the new block.

The objective of the new ModelTransformation is described below:

===== Start of Objective =====
${ #this.parameters.objective }
===== End of Objective =====

Design the ModelTransformation so that executing it achieves this objective.

Determine the required structure of the ModelTransformation from the objective.

Define only the properties that are needed by the transformation and bind their values to the appropriate sources.

Determine how many operations are required to achieve the objective. Use the smallest number of operations that results in a clear and reliable transformation.

For each operation, define its responsibility clearly and ensure that the operations together form a coherent execution flow.

The resulting block must be a complete and valid ModelTransformation definition.</instructions>
            </workflow:InstructionTask>
          </task>
        </workflow:AgenticOperation>
      </composition>
    </operations>
  </aggregations>
  <subBlocks>
    <Parameters>
      <baseType>
        type:StructType
      </baseType>
      <is>
        Run parameters for this transformation
      </is>
      <properties>
        <fqn type="type:TypeIdentifier">
          <documentation>
            The FQN of the new transformation
          </documentation>
        </fqn>
        <objective type="type:Text">
          <documentation>
            The objective of the new transformation
          </documentation>
        </objective>
      </properties>
    </Parameters>
  </subBlocks>
</program:CreateTransformation>
